.nh
.TH "BOSUN" "1" "Jul 2026" "bosun" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
bosun \- Automate SDLC lifecycle tasks

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbosun\fP [\fIflags\fP] [\fIcommand\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Automate SDLC lifecycle tasks

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-a\fP, \fB\-\-approve\fP
Approve the plan without prompting.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fP
Show what would happen without making changes.
.TP
\fB\-\-interactive\fP
Prompt for configurable values.
.TP
\fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP
Display help and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fP, \fB\-\-version\fP
Display version and exit.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBcreate\fP
Create a new issue
.TP
\fBstart\fP
Begin work on an issue
.TP
\fBreview\fP
Submit issue for code review
.TP
\fBpreview\fP
Deploy to preview environment
.TP
\fBprerelease\fP
Prepare release artifacts
.TP
\fBrelease\fP
Deploy to production
.TP
\fBcleanup\fP
Tear down a workspace's previews, branches, and worktrees
.TP
\fBconfig\fP
View and manage bosun configuration
.TP
\fBdoctor\fP
Check bosun configuration and connectivity
.TP
\fBinit\fP
Initialize a new bosun project
.TP
\fBstatus\fP
Show what wants your attention at workspace or project scope
.TP
\fBworkspace\fP
Manage git worktree workspaces

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success.
.TP
1
An error occurred.

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBbash\fP(1), \fBzsh\fP(1), \fBfish\fP(1)
